From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:05:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Slide through captures on the selected item of a grid

A new theme element, <slideshow>, shows captures one at a time at whole-pixel
scales: the smallest of 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2, 3 and 4 at which the capture's region of
interest (<roi>, fractions of the capture) covers the element, centred, and at 2x
and up on the capture's pixel grid, so pixel art stays sharp and an LCD grid drawn
over it lines up.

In a grid's item template it moves only on the selected item: every <interval>
seconds (4 by default) the next capture slides in from the right in <duration>
seconds (0.6), loaded while the current one shows; the other items show the first
capture, and an item that loses the selection goes back to it. Position dots
(<dots>) show at most <maxDots> (9) in a window that follows the current capture,
smaller at an end with more captures beyond. Child elements are drawn over the
captures and the dots over them, so a card's frame or screen filter can sit
between the two. <color> and <saturation> tint the captures; <roundCorners>
clips them.

<path> lists the captures, one per line, and can be bound. ES versions with the
element support the theme feature "slideshow".
